**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** The Henke compound calculator is a third `MaterialSourceProxy`: its snapshot is CXRO's per-element factor files, fetched once and kept in the sources folder, and a record is a compound it computes (the S13.2 brief 'CXRO atomic scattering factors f1, f2 per element are fetched once through the proxy and kept in the snapshot folder'; 'With a chemical formula and a density they give n, k ... as a tabulated user material with provenance (CXRO, citation)'). Verified 2026-11-04 (henke.lbl.gov/optical_constants/asf.html and `sf/si.nff`): one tab-delimited file per element, H to U, at `https://henke.lbl.gov/optical_constants/sf/<symbol in lower case>.nff`; its first line is `E(eV)\tf1\tf2`; each row an energy and f1, f2, plain or with an exponent (`0.186679E-02`); below about 29 eV f1 is the sentinel `-9999.`. CXRO states no licence and cites B. L. Henke, E. M. Gullikson and J. C. Davis, Atomic Data and Nuclear Data Tables 54, 181-342 (1993). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`: `HenkeScatteringText of string` with `.value`, one `.nff` file's text, and `type HenkeScatteringText with member this.factors : Result<AtomicScatteringFactors, ImportError>` (step 456): the first non-empty line MUST start with `E(eV)`; every further non-empty line is three numbers split on tabs and spaces, read with the invariant culture; a row whose f1 is -9999 is left out (CXRO's mark of no f1); the columns go through `AtomicScatteringFactors.tryCreate`, whose refusal, a header that is not CXRO's and a row that does not read are `MalformedSourceFileErr` (step 454) naming the 1-based line; no row left is `NoDataErr`; every .NET call that throws is caught and answered `MalformedSourceFileErr`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialSourceStore.fs`: `type MaterialSourceProxy with static member createHenkeCompounds (sources : FolderName) (downloader : SourceArchiveDownloader) (clock : ClockProvider) : MaterialSourceProxy`, unique on its receiver. Building it touches nothing. `sourceName` is `MaterialSourceName "CXRO Henke"`, the layout's folder (step 455) `<sources>/cxro-henke`, the licence `EntryLicence "LicenseRef-CXRO"` (SPDX's form for a licence it does not list) and the base `https://henke.lbl.gov/optical_constants/sf/`, each written there alone; an element's file is `<symbol in lower case>.nff`. `snapshotVersion` is the layout's. `updateSnapshot observer`: leftovers of an interrupted run are deleted and `<folder>.tmp` is created; then for each of `ChemicalElement.all` in order, the cancellation read first (cancelled: the staged folder deleted, `SourceSnapshotCancelled`), `downloader.downloadArchive` (step 447's one HTTP seam, unchanged) of `SourceArchiveUrl <base><file>` into `<folder>.tmp/<file>` with the token: a cancelled token then answers `SourceSnapshotCancelled`, a download error is answered as it is, and a file whose text `HenkeScatteringText.factors` refuses is `SourceArchiveInvalidErr` naming the element and the error's `describe`, each deleting the staged folder; after each file `reportSnapshotProgress { filesDone = <i>; filesTotal = SourceSnapshotFileCount 92 }`. Once every file is fetched, the layout's `installFrom` with 92 files answers `SourceSnapshotUpdated`; every exception deletes what the run made and keeps the held snapshot (`SourceSnapshotIoErr`). `searchRecords query`: `heldVersion`; `CompoundSpec.tryOfQuery query` (step 456), whose error is `SourceRecordUnreadableErr` carrying its `describe`; an element of the formula without its file in the snapshot is `SourceRecordMissingErr` naming the symbol; otherwise the one hit `{ record = spec.recordId; name = spec.entryName }`: the compound the query writes, because this source has no catalog to filter. `fetchRecord record`: `heldVersion`; `CompoundSpec.tryOfRecord` (an error `SourceRecordMissingErr` naming the record); each element's file read as bytes (missing: `SourceRecordMissingErr`) and through `HenkeScatteringText.factors` (an error `SourceRecordUnreadableErr`); `indexTableWith` (an error `SourceRecordUnreadableErr` carrying its `describe`); and the answer `{ pull = { source; record; recordHash; sourceVersion = <the stamp's>; licence; citation }; material = table.isotropicEntry spec.entryName CategoryIds.semiconductor (EntryDescription "Computed from CXRO atomic scattering factors (Henke, Gullikson and Davis 1993) for <formula text> at <density> g/cm³.") }` (step 454), where `recordHash` is `ContentHash.ofBytes` of the record's UTF-8 text followed by each formula element's file bytes in formula order, so an update that changes an element's factors changes the hash (step 444's rule), and the citation is `EntryCitation "B.L. Henke, E.M. Gullikson and J.C. Davis, Atomic Data and Nuclear Data Tables 54, 181-342 (1993); CXRO atomic scattering factors (henke.lbl.gov/optical_constants): <formula text> at <density> g/cm³"`. No archive download, retry, cache or setting is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialSources.fs`: the `MaterialSourceProxy` doc names `createHenkeCompounds`, and `searchRecords`' field doc (step 443) adds, in one line, that a source without a catalog answers the record its query names. (4) Fixtures: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/si.nff` and `fixtures/o.nff`, `Content` items copied `PreserveNewest` beside `fixtures/ptb-Co.txt`'s with no comment, in CXRO's format with test-local values (not CXRO data): `si.nff` holds the header, `10.0000\t-9999.\t3.94844`, then 100, 200 and 300 eV with f1 10, 12, 13 and f2 2, 1 and `0.500000E+00`; `o.nff` the header, a sentinel row and 150, 250 and 400 eV with f1 6, 7, 7.5 and f2 3, 2, 1, step 456's tables. `MaterialSourceFixture` (step 447) gains, each with a one-line doc: `henkeFile (symbol : string) : byte[]`, the fixture's bytes for `si` and `o` and, for every other element, a test-local header and two rows; `writeHenkeSnapshot (snapshot : string) : unit`, `si.nff`, `o.nff` and the stamp of `2026-11-01`; and `servingDownloader (serve : SourceArchiveUrl -> byte[] option) (asked : ResizeArray<SourceArchiveUrl>) : SourceArchiveDownloader`, which records each URL and writes the served bytes into the target file, answering `SourceDownloadErr "404"` for `None`. Tests: `MaterialImportTests` gains `a CXRO scattering-factor file reads its energies and factors, leaving out the rows without f1`: `fixtures/si.nff` reads 100, 200 and 300 eV with their factors, the sentinel row left out and the exponent read; a text whose first line is `Energy` and one with a row `200 x 1` answer `MalformedSourceFileErr`; a header alone answers `NoDataErr`. `MaterialSourceStoreTests` gains, each over a fresh sources folder: `a Henke compound source without a snapshot answers no version and refuses search and fetch`; `a Henke update downloads every element's factors once, file by file, and installs them`: over a held snapshot, `updateSnapshot` with `servingDownloader` of `henkeFile` and `fixedClock` of 2026-11-04 asks 92 URLs, the first `https://henke.lbl.gov/optical_constants/sf/h.nff` and the last `.../sf/u.nff`, in atomic-number order, reports 1 to 92 of 92, answers `SourceSnapshotUpdated` of `2026-11-04` and 92 files, and leaves the snapshot holding exactly the 92 `.nff` files and `.snapshot-json` and the sources folder nothing else; `a Henke update cancelled before its next element, or failing on one, keeps the held snapshot`: a token cancelled on the first progress answers `SourceSnapshotCancelled`, and a downloader serving `None` for `fe` answers `SourceDownloadErr`, each leaving the held snapshot byte for byte and nothing beside it; `a Henke search names the compound its query writes, and refuses a query that names none`: over `writeHenkeSnapshot`, `SiO2 2.2` finds one hit `SiO2@2.2` named `SiO2, ρ = 2.2 g/cm³ (CXRO Henke)`, `SiO2` answers `SourceRecordUnreadableErr` and `Fe2O3 5.2` `SourceRecordMissingErr` naming `Fe`; `a fetched Henke compound is the index its elements' factors give, under CXRO's provenance`: the fetched `SiO2@2.2` holds the table `indexTableWith` gives over the two fixture files read through `factors`, under that name, the hash of `SiO2@2.2`'s bytes followed by `si.nff`'s and `o.nff`'s, `2026-11-04`, `LicenseRef-CXRO` and the citation above.

**Acceptance.** After the adapter lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `MaterialSourceProxy.createHenkeCompounds` over a fixture snapshot under the test output, its update MUST fetch the 92 element files once, file by file, through the one HTTP seam's shape, its search MUST name the compound its query writes, and its fetch MUST compute the compound's table through `indexTableWith` under CXRO's provenance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a CXRO scattering-factor file reads its energies and factors, leaving out the rows without f1`, `a Henke compound source without a snapshot answers no version and refuses search and fetch`, `a Henke update downloads every element's factors once, file by file, and installs them`, `a Henke update cancelled before its next element, or failing on one, keeps the held snapshot`, `a Henke search names the compound its query writes, and refuses a query that names none` and `a fetched Henke compound is the index its elements' factors give, under CXRO's provenance`, the count rising by 6; kit-acceptance MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with AT-1 and AT-2 expectations and tolerances unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
